      "writtenOn": "2023-11-02T09:12:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Suren,\nWe discussed about upstream and we found it is really hard. In our codes, we will use the hooks like this:\n\u0027\u0027\u0027\nvoid vendor_hook_callback_func()\n{\n    if (current_is_key_task())\n        do_our_optimize_work();\n}\n\u0027\u0027\u0027\nWe rely on external symbol \u0027current_is_key_task\u0027 to determine which thread is important for user experience. That symbol is provided by other kernel module and works with user-space strategy. These codes belong to different groups, we don\u0027t have ownership. So we can\u0027t upstream our feature unless they upstream theirs and we still need these hooks.",
      "parentUuid": "8de87552_dc5778da",
      "revId": "ef8076ac0a79b7d18ec7d28170b523fd17ca2be3",
